      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Vrchat cannot fix this, this is unity. I don't think unity could really do much though as the reason it crashes is because your computer runs out of memory for converting all the assets. Too many assets -> not enough memory.\n\n I will say that for my larger projects, it's quicker to switch build and then force crash unity via task manager and reopen the project. The project will be in the correct build mode and you won't crash other software on your computer.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
